.el .ds Aq '
.TH ag-remote 1  "remote 0.2.0-rc.1" 
.SH NAME
ag\-remote \- Manage remotes and work with proposals, events and policy on a server
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBag remote\fR [\fB\-C\fR|\fB\-\-repo\fR] [\fB\-\-remote\fR] [\fB\-\-as\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-\-color\fR] [\fB\-q\fR|\fB\-\-quiet\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Manage remotes and work with proposals, events and policy on a server
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-C\fR, \fB\-\-repo\fR \fI<DIR>\fR
Operate on the repository at this path (default: discovered from the current directory)
.TP
\fB\-\-remote\fR \fI<REMOTE>\fR
Remote to use (default: origin)
.TP
\fB\-\-as\fR \fI<IDENTITY>\fR
Act as this identity (`user:alice`, `agent:bot#run_…`, `service:ci`). Also: AG_IDENTITY
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Machine\-readable JSON output
.TP
\fB\-\-color\fR \fI<WHEN>\fR
Colour the output: auto (a terminal, unless NO_COLOR is set), always or never
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Print only what was asked for: no confirmations or hints. Errors and refusals are still shown
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Explain what is happening on standard error: repository, identity, remote, timing
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
ag\-remote\-add(1)
Add a remote
.TP
ag\-remote\-list(1)
List remotes
.TP
ag\-remote\-remove(1)
Forget a remote
.TP
ag\-remote\-whoami(1)
Show who the server thinks you are
.TP
ag\-remote\-proposals(1)
List proposals on the server
.TP
ag\-remote\-proposal(1)
Show a proposal with its reviews
.TP
ag\-remote\-prepare(1)
What would integrating do now, and what is missing?
.TP
ag\-remote\-review(1)
Review a proposal\*(Aqs current head
.TP
ag\-remote\-integrate(1)
Integrate a proposal into its stream
.TP
ag\-remote\-close(1)
Close a proposal without integrating it
.TP
ag\-remote\-streams(1)
List streams
.TP
ag\-remote\-events(1)
Show the events of the repository (replay), or follow them live
.TP
ag\-remote\-policy(1)
Show or set a stream\*(Aqs policy
.TP
ag\-remote\-log(1)
Show history of a revision on the server
.TP
ag\-remote\-blame(1)
Show which changeset introduced each line of a file on the server: `ag remote blame main:src/lib.rs`
.TP
ag\-remote\-cat(1)
Print a file as of a revision on the server: `ag remote cat main:src/lib.rs`
.SH VERSION
v0.2.0\-rc.1
